# Netscape HTTP Cookie File
#
# YouTube cookies for yt-dlp. Optional — YouTube downloads work without this
# until a host gets flagged with "Sign in to confirm you're not a bot", at which
# point yt-dlp needs a logged-in session to keep working.
#
# docker-compose.yml bind-mounts ./cookies.txt into the container. Docker
# creates a DIRECTORY at that path if the file is missing, which breaks the
# mount — so copy this file before your first `docker compose up`:
#
#     cp cookies.txt.example cookies.txt
#
# An empty file is fine. To populate it, export cookies for youtube.com from a
# browser where you're signed in (any "Netscape HTTP Cookie File" exporter), or
# run:  yt-dlp --cookies-from-browser chrome --cookies cookies.txt
#
# NEVER commit the filled-in cookies.txt — .gitignore already excludes it.
